.page yes 1 repeat a line forever

# SYNOPSIS
*yes* [_STRING_]

# DESCRIPTION
`yes` writes _STRING_ (or `y`) followed by a newline, over and over, until it is killed or whoever reads it goes away. Only the first argument is used.

# EXAMPLES
    yes | head -3
    yes "n" | rm -i *.tmp

# SEE ALSO
seq(1), head(1)
